<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Clinical program priorities">
  <div><strong>Start with the use case</strong><span>Define the population, setting, hydration problem and outcome before considering a product claim.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Feasibility first</strong><span>Preparation, adherence, measurements and workflow need to work before a larger study makes sense.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Predefine the next step</strong><span>Results should determine whether to refine, stop, repeat or advance.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Program pillars</p>
  <h2>What we need to understand</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4">
    <article><h3>Measurement</h3><p>Which hydration measures are practical and interpretable in the population being studied?</p></article>
    <article><h3>Preparation & tolerance</h3><p>Can the product be prepared consistently, consumed as intended and tolerated?</p></article>
    <article><h3>Clinical relevance</h3><p>Are the outcomes meaningful to the care question, not just easy to measure?</p></article>
    <article><h3>Implementation</h3><p>Can the approach fit real workflows, staffing, education and access?</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__feature">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Evidence ladder</p>
    <h2>Advance only when the previous question is answered</h2>
    <p>Rationale asks whether the idea is plausible. Feasibility asks whether the study can work. Safety and tolerability ask whether the intervention can be used as planned. Efficacy asks whether it changes a predefined outcome. Implementation asks whether any benefit survives real-world use.</p>
    <p>Later-stage clinical language should not outrun the strongest evidence available.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Governance</p>
    <h2>The protocol determines the requirements</h2>
    <p>Human research should define investigator and sponsor roles, data custody, safety reporting, analysis, conflicts of interest and publication plans before the work begins.</p>
    <p>Research Ethics Board and regulatory requirements depend on what the study actually does. Calling a project “observational” or “pilot” does not change requirements triggered by the protocol.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Claim rule</span>
    <h3>Question first. Claim later.</h3>
    <p>Separate what physiology suggests, what the label authorizes, what a study tests and what completed results show.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Decision gates</p>
  <h2>What happens next?</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Main question</th><th>Possible next step</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Methods / feasibility</strong></td><td>Can the protocol be executed and measured reliably?</td><td>Refine methods, reduce burden or advance.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Pilot</strong></td><td>Are recruitment, preparation, adherence and safety monitoring workable?</td><td>Stop, redesign, narrow or plan a larger study.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Controlled evaluation</strong></td><td>Does the intervention change the prespecified outcome?</td><td>Replicate, refine or stop.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Implementation</strong></td><td>Can it be delivered appropriately in real care?</td><td>Refine workflow, access and eligibility.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__brand-context">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Current stage</p>
    <h2>Methods and feasibility come first</h2>
    <p>Our public clinical-development language remains conservative while measurement, governance and pilot-study foundations are being built.</p>
